{"kind":"report","text":"CHANGES-REQUESTED at exact clean head e592fcd28c094fd63d4db24706afc1a22c553c76. Four findings. (1) Admission clauses do not bound GitHub reads in the command: cmd/gitseq-github/main.go always calls Client.Issues once for the whole repository, Client.Issues always paginates state=all, Clause.Query is unused outside its unit test, and Admit receives nil labels. A selection clause therefore reads every issue, while any label criterion can never admit anything. This contradicts the charter's scale boundary and the advertised criteria form. (2) github.Namespace is dead. appendObservation passes only IdempotencyKey into Workspace.BuildActRequest, which signs with the workroom-wide Config.IdempotencyNamespace (normally workroom/v0). No signed connector act uses connector/github@0, so the stated collision boundary and charter mapping are false and future connector operations by the same actor can collide. (3) charterIsLive checks only that the named statement is ratified, live and present. It accepts any ratified statement kind and never binds the charter's repository, connector actor or mapping to --owner, --repo-name and --as. The command can therefore observe a different repository under an unrelated ratified statement while claiming the charter is its doorstep. (4) the claimed comment read-back defence is not on an executable path: ObserveComment and Owned are referenced only by tests, no comment fetch or command path exists, and Owned is only a public marker prefix that any GitHub commenter can write, despite the claim that the structure is connector-only. Focused package tests and vet pass, but they do not exercise these integration boundaries.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:8130a34ca147dc9f7cb472015c7507aad99563c8","conditions":"Wire clause-specific source queries and label data; sign the declared connector namespace; validate charter identity and scope against the invocation; make comment ownership executable and non-spoofable or narrow the claims and chartered surface.","findings":"4","head":"e592fcd28c094fd63d4db24706afc1a22c553c76","tests":"go test ./internal/connector/github ./cmd/gitseq-github; go vet ./internal/connector/github ./cmd/gitseq-github","verdict":"changes-requested"}}